acks the rook on h8, which is undefended."],"better":"16.Qg7 threatens Qxh8+, winning a rook, and stops …bxc3. After 16…Rf8 17.c4 b3+ 18.Ke2 bxa2 19.Nc6, White is a pawn down (+1.12)."},{"ply":41,"name":"21.Nd5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"21.Nd5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked knight to safety.","Centralises the knight on d5, where it reaches the most squares.","The next best move, 21.Nc6, would drop White's winning chances from 49% to 35% (−1.73).","21.Nd5 gets the knight out of the way of …axb4 and threatens Nc7+, winning the exchange, picking it up with 22.Nxa8.","Black was threatening …axb4, winning a knight for a pawn. The knight steps away.","It threatens Nc7+, winning the exchange, picking it up with 22.Nxa8, so Black has to spend the next move on it."]},{"ply":85,"name":"43.Rc8","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"43.Rc8 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 27% to 13%.","points":["Black answers 43…Kf4.","Better was 43.g3 (−2.65): makes an escape square for the king, so back-rank checks lose their sting."],"better":"43.g3 makes luft for the king. After 43…Ke4 44.Kg1 e5 45.h5 Rxc4 46.Rd1, White is a pawn down (−2.65)."},{"ply":86,"name":"43…Kf4","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"43…Kf4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 43…g3, would drop Black's winning chances from 87% to 76% (−3.17).","43…Kf4 prepares …Kg3 and …Rc1+.","The engine's plan continues with …Kg3 and …Rc1+: this move is the first step.","White answers 44.Rb8.","After 44.Rb8 Kg3 45.h5 Rc1+ 46.Ke2 Rxc4 47.Kd3, Black comes out a pawn up (−5.06)."]},{"ply":92,"name":"46…Rc1+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"46…Rc1+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Check, and White has only one legal reply.","The next best move, 46…f3, would drop Black's winning chances from 85% to 24% (+3.11).","46…Rc1+ gives check, leaving one